# Allowlist: only own-authored content is versioned.
# Third-party skills (matt-pocock via `npx skills`, etc.) live in this same
# directory and stay out of version control.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/.claude-plugin
!/tk
!/tk-cowork
!/plugin-drift
!/asr
!/githooks
!/bin

# Agent config, versioned so that `git worktree add` materialises it (README, "Layout").
# The four rules run in order: reopen docs/, close what sits directly inside it, reopen
# agents/, close that too — then name the three files `/setup-matt-pocock-skills` writes.
# Naming them rather than opening the directory is what keeps the next file dropped there
# from reaching a PUBLIC repo on its own.
!/docs
/docs/*
!/docs/agents
/docs/agents/*
!/docs/agents/issue-tracker.md
!/docs/agents/triage-labels.md
!/docs/agents/domain.md

# Pruning baselines and the script that lays them out (T185). Named file by file
# for the reason the block above is: a pruning report on a PRIVATE skill must not
# reach this PUBLIC repo, and an open `!/docs/prune` would let `git add -A` carry
# one in. The gitignore is the first line here, the pre-commit guard the second.
!/docs/prune
/docs/prune/*
!/docs/prune/baseline.py
!/docs/prune/baseline-2026-08-27.md

# The hookify stop rule that this repo's own sessions run under, versioned so that
# `git worktree add` materialises it — an unversioned copy leaves every worktree of this
# repo with no guard at all. Named file by file for the same reason as the blocks above:
# `.claude/*.local.md` is where a LOCAL rule lands, and an open `!/.claude` would let one
# carrying private values reach this PUBLIC repo.
!/.claude
/.claude/*
!/.claude/hookify.code-review-antes-de-pronto.local.md

# Python bytecode from the test suites
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# pytest's own cache dir (tk/tests/) — named explicitly so this .gitignore,
# not the .gitignore pytest writes inside the dir, is the one that ignores it
.pytest_cache/
